# Real-Postgres runtime proof for body+finish commit ambiguity recovery.
register_gate "tests/test_atomic_delivery_finalize_pg.py" "ATOMIC DELIVERY FINALIZE POSTGRES GATE: PASS" "real-Postgres one-transaction delivery finalization" "a scratch production schema drives DeliveryStore.wrap_processor(make_db_processor) through the actual App role: an instrumented connection lets body writes plus exact finish commit server-side and then lose only the ACK; the wrapper resolves done as processed, performs no separate finish, and a duplicate observation executes no body. A second connection fails before COMMIT and proves both body writes and staged finish roll back before the resolver returns the exact lease to queued." "runtime wiring—not only the SQL resolver in isolation—prevents committed webhook replay and preserves rollback-safe retry"
